      "writtenOn": "2019-08-16T16:36:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would we avoid upstream allergic reactions if we talk about this as a pack vs spread policy instead of latency sensitivity? We don\u0027t want to be dismissed with \"if it\u0027s latency sensitive then use RT or DL?\" argument. Spread (default non-EAS behavior) vs pack (common EAS behavior) seems like a very legitimate policy hint.",
      "revId": "f667511c769e4814e45319553946371ec3327178",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
